{
  "title": "Operation Silent Script",
  "levels": [
    {
      "title": "1. Infiltration",
      "instructions": "HQ: Grep Fox, you're inside. Your target is one data chip. Each floor panel is 100 steps wide, and `step(100)` won't get you all the way. Adjust the number and press Run.",
      "starterCode": "step(100)\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": {
          "x": 100,
          "y": 250,
          "angle": 0
        },
        "chips": [
          {
            "x": 400,
            "y": 250
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Blind Corner",
      "instructions": "HQ: Crates ahead, and you can't go through them. Go around. `turn(90)` turns right and `turn(-90)` turns left.",
      "starterCode": "step(400)\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": {
          "x": 100,
          "y": 400,
          "angle": 0
        },
        "chips": [
          {
            "x": 500,
            "y": 150
          }
        ],
        "obstacles": [
          {
            "x": 200,
            "y": 150,
            "w": 200,
            "h": 180
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Crate Alley",
      "instructions": "HQ: Four chips in this alley. Collect them in order. You can give as many orders as you need, one on each line.",
      "starterCode": "step(200)\nturn(-90)\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": {
          "x": 100,
          "y": 400,
          "angle": 0
        },
        "chips": [
          {
            "x": 300,
            "y": 400
          },
          {
            "x": 300,
            "y": 250
          },
          {
            "x": 500,
            "y": 250
          },
          {
            "x": 500,
            "y": 100
          }
        ],
        "obstacles": [
          {
            "x": 100,
            "y": 100,
            "w": 150,
            "h": 200
          },
          {
            "x": 350,
            "y": 300,
            "w": 250,
            "h": 150
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "4. Service Stairs",
      "instructions": "HQ: These stairs repeat, so don't write every order. Put one stair inside a `for` loop: move 100 steps, turn left, move 75 steps, turn right.",
      "starterCode": "for i in range(5):\n    step(100)\n    # add the rest of one stair here\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": {
          "x": 100,
          "y": 450,
          "angle": 0
        },
        "chips": [
          {
            "x": 200,
            "y": 375
          },
          {
            "x": 300,
            "y": 300
          },
          {
            "x": 400,
            "y": 225
          },
          {
            "x": 500,
            "y": 150
          },
          {
            "x": 600,
            "y": 75
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "5. Perimeter Sweep",
      "instructions": "HQ: Sweep the perimeter around the crate. Each side is the same, so one loop can handle the whole patrol.",
      "starterCode": "for i in range(4):\n    # walk one side, then turn the corner\n    pass\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 100,
          "angle": 0
        },
        "chips": [
          {
            "x": 500,
            "y": 100
          },
          {
            "x": 500,
            "y": 400
          },
          {
            "x": 200,
            "y": 400
          }
        ],
        "obstacles": [
          {
            "x": 300,
            "y": 180,
            "w": 100,
            "h": 140
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Searchlight Yard",
      "instructions": "HQ: Stay out of the searchlight. The chips form a hexagon around it: each side is 150 steps and each corner is a 60 degree turn.",
      "starterCode": "for i in range(6):\n    step(150)\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": {
          "x": 325,
          "y": 100,
          "angle": 0
        },
        "chips": [
          {
            "x": 475,
            "y": 100
          },
          {
            "x": 550,
            "y": 230
          },
          {
            "x": 475,
            "y": 360
          },
          {
            "x": 325,
            "y": 360
          },
          {
            "x": 250,
            "y": 230
          }
        ],
        "hazards": [
          {
            "x": 400,
            "y": 230,
            "r": 50
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "7. Target List",
      "instructions": "HQ: Here's your target list. `chips` holds every chip in the room. `turn_to(c)` faces a chip and `distance_to(c)` tells you how far away it is, so you never need to measure.",
      "starterCode": "for c in chips:\n    turn_to(c)\n    # now walk to the chip\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": {
          "x": 100,
          "y": 100,
          "angle": 0
        },
        "chips": [
          {
            "x": 300,
            "y": 150
          },
          {
            "x": 500,
            "y": 100
          },
          {
            "x": 700,
            "y": 200
          },
          {
            "x": 500,
            "y": 350
          },
          {
            "x": 200,
            "y": 400
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "8. Standard Procedure",
      "instructions": "HQ: Time for a standard procedure. A function gives a name to orders you use often. Fill in `grab`, then choose your route carefully: `chips[0]` is across the searchlight, so start with the chip nearest you.",
      "starterCode": "def grab(chip):\n    turn_to(chip)\n    # walk to the chip\n\ngrab(chips[0])\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": {
          "x": 100,
          "y": 250,
          "angle": 0
        },
        "chips": [
          {
            "x": 700,
            "y": 250
          },
          {
            "x": 550,
            "y": 100
          },
          {
            "x": 250,
            "y": 100
          }
        ],
        "hazards": [
          {
            "x": 400,
            "y": 250,
            "r": 100
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "9. Recon Grid",
      "instructions": "HQ: Functions can take inputs. Finish `square(size)`, sweep the small square, take 200 steps to reach the big one, then sweep that too.",
      "starterCode": "def square(size):\n    for i in range(4):\n        step(size)\n        # turn the corner\n\nsquare(100)\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": {
          "x": 100,
          "y": 100,
          "angle": 0
        },
        "chips": [
          {
            "x": 200,
            "y": 100
